{"ts":"2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9b054e739855a3b67742faac","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-a8zm","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Trust boundary\n\n- Discover and pin authorization-server issuer identity before persisting or redeeming credentials.\n- Validate a returned iss value and never reuse credentials across issuers.\n- Send an appropriate application_type and prefer Client ID Metadata Documents over deprecated dynamic registration.\n- Make consent scopes align with pm read, mutation, workspace, extension, task, and resource authority.\n- Validate transport headers and custom x-mcp-header mappings against injection, confused deputy, SSRF, replay, downgrade, and proxy-cache threats.\n- Propagate traceparent, tracestate, and baggage only through allowlisted metadata with privacy limits and redaction.\n- Keep stdio local trust behavior distinct from remote HTTP authorization rather than silently treating one as the other."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-3zh9s4"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"MCP remote authorization and observability: issuer-bound credentials, client metadata documents, consent, header security, and OpenTelemetry propagation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Define and implement the 2026-07-28 remote MCP trust boundary for Streamable HTTP, including authorization discovery, issuer validation, registration migration, consent, trace context, and abuse resistance."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:mcp","authorization","client-metadata","issuer","oauth","opentelemetry","privacy","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/deadline","value":"2026-11-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":960},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Authorization-server discovery and issuer pinning prevent credentials from being reused or redeemed at a different issuer; Present iss values are validated and dynamic registration fallback is bounded behind Client ID Metadata Document preference; application_type, redirect URI, scopes, consent, refresh, revocation, and re-registration behavior have positive and negative tests; Header mappings, proxies, caches, traces, logs, errors, and telemetry cannot leak tokens, secrets, workspace paths, or private resource content; traceparent, tracestate, and baggage propagation follows explicit allowlists, byte limits, and redaction; A threat model and real Streamable HTTP integration suite gate release"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"Secure observable remote pm MCP"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make every remote request attributable, authorized, consented, privacy-bounded, and traceable without credential or context leakage"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Organizations can expose pm remotely without unsafe token reuse, redirect ambiguity, header injection, or opaque failures"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The revision tightens issuer and application-type validation, binds credentials to authorization servers, prefers Client ID Metadata Documents, and defines trace-context propagation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-rs9vry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1jzupz","kind":"verifies","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-sqvshj","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-v7e337","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-25T05:10:30.953Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for MCP authorization iss issuer binding application_type client ID metadata documents dynamic registration consent headers and OpenTelemetry. No current item owns the remote 2026-07-28 trust boundary."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"963f54cf7ca03a8c3b7abaaae7c4726db5f774abb27e6fbe6b1887f563b7c31d","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
